  choices = $EXPL$["A forensic image captures all data including deleted files and slack space, unlike a standard backup","A forensic image compresses data more efficiently and produces smaller output files","A standard backup captures more data because it includes full application configurations","A forensic image and standard backup are functionally identical in scope and content"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Per NIST SP 800-86, Section 4.2, a forensic image is a bit-for-bit copy of the entire storage device, capturing deleted files, slack space, and unallocated areas. This preserves all potential evidence that a standard backup of active files would miss.
Wrong (B): Forensic images are typically larger than standard backups because they capture the entire disk, not a compressed subset.
